---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { markdownResponse } from "../lib/markdown";

const markdown = `# Alejandro Ramírez

Automation and Integrations Engineer based in Berlin. I turn repeated manual operations and fragile toolchains into reliable, traceable systems.

I build API integrations, workflow automation, document processing, accounting systems, data pipelines, internal tools, and backend services. My day-to-day toolkit includes n8n, Make, Python, SQL, Docker, APIs, and Unix systems.

## Selected technical tutorials

- [Fail-closed SumUp to Lexware accounting](https://soyalejo.com/work/sumup-lexware-fail-closed): Reconcile a business day before creating financial records.
- [Idempotent supplier PDF ingestion](https://soyalejo.com/work/hamberger-invoices-lexware): Parse German supplier invoices, preserve tax buckets, and attach source evidence.
- [Payout evidence attachment](https://soyalejo.com/work/payout-evidence-attachments): Match a payout PDF to the correct voucher without hiding ambiguity.
- [Public-record intake](https://soyalejo.com/work/jurisdata-ticket-intake): Retrieve structured public data, route approved guidance, and keep retries duplicate-safe.
- [hamberger-dl](https://soyalejo.com/work/hamberger-dl): An open-source CLI for supplier invoice retrieval with OIDC, filters, ZIP export, and safe re-runs.

## Background

At Ko Kitchen, I build accounting, invoice, and operations automation. Before that, I co-founded JurisDATA, where an automated intake and guidance workflow helped more than 50,000 people. At 42 Berlin, I studied C, C++, Unix, networking, concurrency, and systems programming.

## Contact

For Automation and Integrations Engineer, Business Systems Engineer, Internal Tools Engineer, or Backend and Integrations Engineer roles, email [faramirezs@gmail.com](mailto:faramirezs@gmail.com). See [GitHub](https://github.com/faramirezs) and [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/in/alejandro-mlops-engineer/).
`;

const markdownPage = Astro.locals.prefersMarkdown ? markdownResponse(markdown) : null;
if (markdownPage) return markdownPage;
const isGerman = Astro.url.searchParams.get("lang") === "de";
---

